.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead label" 1  "bead label " 
.SH NAME
bead label \- Manage labels
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead label\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add or remove labels on an issue.
.PP
Labels are free\-form, case\-sensitive strings used for categorization. Both
operations are idempotent, so they are safe to run repeatedly.
.PP
  bead label add <ID> \-\-label <LABEL>
  bead label remove <ID> \-\-label <LABEL>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bead label\-add(1)
Add a label to an issue
.TP
bead label\-remove(1)
Remove a label from an issue
.TP
bead label\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
